//! This manifold deploys a migration model on two processes. The entry process
//! runs `main` at `near`.
//!
//! A manifold binds the worlds of a program onto sites. So one program runs as
//! two processes. Its source names neither process.
//!
//! The manifold deploys the migration model beside it and binds `far` to the
//! imported site. The model of that site holds the key and the socket. The
//! manifold places `near` nowhere. `gandr run --manifold` and
//! `gandr host --manifold` read the manifold as the
//! `--world far=<key>@<ip:port>` that it desugars to. `gandr check` of the
//! manifold resolves `far` against the worlds of the program.
//!
//! - see: `two-processes.gandr`
import std.manifold (Site, Manifold, Placement, At);
import "./two-processes.site.gandr" as far;
import std.list (List);

/// The program this manifold deploys.
pub module Manifold : Model(Manifold) where
  /// The migration model, beside this file.
  def artifact = "two-processes.gandr";

/// `far` at the far site, as one process.
pub def placements : List Placement = #[
  At "far" far.site,
];
